| frabrl.hct 1;2 - hyphenation control tbl for French text
| 1;1 1988-2-9 JES (derived from dash.hct)
| 1;2 1994-9-16/20 JES: handle lowercase letters as well as u.c., which is
|     necessary for new .brx files (since there is no internal upcasing, as
|     with former .sct-based scanning)
-hinit 1
| hyphenation mode:
|   0 = no breaks whatsoever (even at dashes)
|   1 = breaks preferably after, possibly before, dashes
|   2 = like 1, but also breaks after internal hyphens
|   3 = Markov algorithm
3
| sequence used for dash (2 chars)
--
| hyphen character
-
| minimum "real" word length to hyphenate at all
4
| minimum length word to leave before break at dash
2
| min to leave before internal hyphen
2
| min to leave before algorithm-break
2
 | spare
 | spare
# | char which, at beginning of wd, excludes it from hy'n (number sign)
| transition-string for beginning-of-word
| !"#$%&'()*+,-./0123456789:;<=>?@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ[\]^_`abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz{|}~
 10000000000010100000000110000000000000000000000000000000000000010000000000000000000000000000000
